# PR Diff Truncated

Original size: 204164 characters.
Kept: first 7800 and last 4200 characters.

The full diff is available in the checked-out PR branch. Use `git diff` or CodeGraph for focused source navigation instead of relying only on this file.

```diff
diff --git a/.github/workflows/ai-teammate.yml b/.github/workflows/ai-teammate.yml
index 3ee9cd2f5..8a2b7233d 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ai-teammate.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ai-teammate.yml
@@ -67,7 +67,10 @@ on:
       leg:
         description: 'Which leg to run'
         type: choice
-        options: [dev, review, rework]
+        # gh-1352: polish — the bounded suggestion-only lap the disposition
+        # loop dispatches on an approved BLOCKED head (top-K threads,
+        # once-per-head, instability-budgeted).
+        options: [dev, review, rework, polish]
       reason:
         description: 'Why (audit trail)'
         type: string
diff --git a/instructions/pr_rework/general_guidelines.md b/instructions/pr_rework/general_guidelines.md
index f0ed3797b..4503d8fa9 100644
--- a/instructions/pr_rework/general_guidelines.md
+++ b/instructions/pr_rework/general_guidelines.md
@@ -93,3 +93,11 @@ You may downgrade a **specific** ⚠️ IMPORTANT finding to 💡 SUGGESTION **o
 - A silent downgrade does not exist — without the written justification the finding stays ⚠️ and the review re-raises it, repeating the loop.
 - Downgrade the finding, not the conversation: still reply to the thread (the reply IS the justification carrier).
 - Never downgrade 🚨 BLOCKING — only the reviewer (or the project `reviewPolicy` config) can weaken a blocking finding.
+
+## 5. Opportunistic pickup — cheap 💡/🪶 ride the lap (gh-1352)
+
+While the lap fixes its mandatory set (🚨/⚠️), pick up the cheap findings you pass anyway:
+
+- **Eligible:** 💡 SUGGESTION / 🪶 NIT findings in the SAME files your mandatory fixes already touch — you are in the file, the change is doc/test-trivial, and the lap budget allows it: `review_policy.md` carries `opportunisticMaxThreads` (default 8) and `opportunisticSameFilesOnly` (default true). Stay inside both.
+- **Not eligible (leave for triage):** findings in files the mandatory set does not touch, findings needing >trivial edits, and anything non-local to this PR's diff. Skipping them is correct — the machine triage closes non-picked threads with `wontfix`/`defered` dispositions after the lap lands; do NOT force-fix them here.
+- **Bookkeeping:** every picked-up thread still gets its `outputs/review_replies.json` entry; name the fixing commit in the reply so the machine can close it as `fixed: <ref>`. Threads you did not pick up need no reply — triage owns them.
diff --git a/js/common/ledgerCore.js b/js/common/ledgerCore.js
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..fcb29bd8e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/js/common/ledgerCore.js
@@ -0,0 +1,276 @@
+/**
+ * ledgerCore.js — the shared ledger+sweep pattern (gh-1352 scope 4).
+ *
+ * The rolling-ledger machinery shipped in gh-1345/gh-1348
+ * (js/common/tcMaintenanceLedger.js + the dispatcher + the suppression
+ * anchors) carried the full append/refresh/reopen/resolve lifecycle and
+ * the batched-sweep trigger as a TC-side singleton. gh-1352 adds the
+ * REVIEW-side debt ledger consumer (deferred review findings) — the same
+ * lifecycle, a different identity scheme — so the pattern is extracted
+ * here and both consumers delegate. Nothing is duplicated a third time.
+ *
+ *   Identity    the consumer owns the id scheme (the TC ledger hashes
+ *               tcKey+errorClass+script; the review ledger keys gh-1332
+ *               finding identities). The core only matches on `id`.
+ *   Lifecycle   open -> resolved (a sweep fixes the batch; resolvedVia
+ *               names it) -> open again on re-occurrence. Append-only
+ *               evidence is never rewritten; dispositions only flip
+ *               status.
+ *   Sweep       the batched-sweep trigger: open count >= sweepBatch
+ *               (10) OR the oldest open item >= sweepMaxAgeDays (30)
+ *               → ONE batched sweep leg → one PR fixing the batch; stale
+ *               items are re-validated and dropped with a note.
+ *
+ * Pure module — no dmtools globals. GraalJS-clean (var + plain functions,
+ * JSON-safe data).
+ */
+'use strict';
+
+// ── shape ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+function emptyLedger(version) {
+    return { v: version, at: new Date().toISOString(), findings: [] };
+}
+
+function deepCopyLedger(l) {
+    return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(l || emptyLedger(1)));
+}
+
+// Marker-hygiene cap for free-text fields (agent-authored evidence can be
+// arbitrarily large; the ledger carries pointers, not essays).
+function truncate(text, max) {
+    var s = String(text || '');
+    var limit = max || 500;
+    return s.length > limit ? s.substring(0, limit) : s;
+}
+
+// The first present (non-null/non-'' /non-undefined) value of the named
+// source keys, in priority order — the consumers' field tables share it.
+function firstDefined(obj, keys) {
+    for (var i = 0; i < keys.length; i++) {
+        if (obj[keys[i]] !== undefined && obj[keys[i]] !== null && obj[keys[i]] !== '') return obj[keys[i]];
+    }
+    return null;
+}
